								Mini-Project-1

1.Installed Jenkins,Maven,Docker

2.created a project using maven 
	cmd :mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=my-app -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -Dinteractiv        eMode=false

	a.Inside src I written a simple code and pushed on to the git hub and given the Jenkins url as webhook and created a feature branch        and pushed a new code on to it

3.Created a Docker File: used to build the image 

4.created a Jenkins pipeline: When ever the code is committed the pipeline starts
	a. installed tools Maven with lates version so that Jenkins can perform maven commands	
	b. intalled git-integratoin-plugin so that Jenkins is notified via git hub webhook
	c.Given credentials for git hub and docekr hub
	d. cloning repo
	e. Using the build tool maven to clean and package the code
	f. using github credentials so that I can push the code to the github
	g. Building the docker image and pushing the image to docker hub using docker hub credentials

